 679:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****   /**
 680:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  @brief  A standard container using fixed-size memory allocation and
 681:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  constant-time manipulation of elements at either end.
 682:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 683:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  @ingroup sequences
 684:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 685:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  @tparam _Tp  Type of element.
 686:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  @tparam _Alloc  Allocator type, defaults to allocator<_Tp>.
 687:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 688:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  Meets the requirements of a <a href="tables.html#65">container</a>, a
 689:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  <a href="tables.html#66">reversible container</a>, and a
 690:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  <a href="tables.html#67">sequence</a>, including the
 691:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  <a href="tables.html#68">optional sequence requirements</a>.
 692:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 693:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  In previous HP/SGI versions of deque, there was an extra template
 694:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  parameter so users could control the node size.  This extension turned
ARM GAS  /var/folders/41/s_9r3f9s4p3_9jgx7wszdkhh0000gn/T//ccDOydHt.s 			page 22


 695:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  out to violate the C++ standard (it can be detected using template
 696:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  template parameters), and it was removed.
 697:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 698:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  Here's how a deque<Tp> manages memory.  Each deque has 4 members:
 699:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 700:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  - Tp**        _M_map
 701:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  - size_t      _M_map_size
 702:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  - iterator    _M_start, _M_finish
 703:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 704:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  map_size is at least 8.  %map is an array of map_size
 705:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  pointers-to-@a nodes.  (The name %map has nothing to do with the
 706:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  std::map class, and @b nodes should not be confused with
 707:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  std::list's usage of @a node.)
 708:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 709:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  A @a node has no specific type name as such, but it is referred
 710:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  to as @a node in this file.  It is a simple array-of-Tp.  If Tp
 711:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  is very large, there will be one Tp element per node (i.e., an
 712:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  @a array of one).  For non-huge Tp's, node size is inversely
 713:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  related to Tp size: the larger the Tp, the fewer Tp's will fit
 714:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  in a node.  The goal here is to keep the total size of a node
 715:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  relatively small and constant over different Tp's, to improve
 716:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  allocator efficiency.
 717:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 718:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  Not every pointer in the %map array will point to a node.  If
 719:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  the initial number of elements in the deque is small, the
 720:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  /middle/ %map pointers will be valid, and the ones at the edges
 721:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  will be unused.  This same situation will arise as the %map
 722:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  grows: available %map pointers, if any, will be on the ends.  As
 723:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  new nodes are created, only a subset of the %map's pointers need
 724:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  to be copied @a outward.
 725:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *
 726:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *  Class invariants:
 727:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * - For any nonsingular iterator i:
 728:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *    - i.node points to a member of the %map array.  (Yes, you read that
 729:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *      correctly:  i.node does not actually point to a node.)  The member of
 730:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *      the %map array is what actually points to the node.
 731:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *    - i.first == *(i.node)    (This points to the node (first Tp element).)
 732:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *    - i.last  == i.first + node_size
 733:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *    - i.cur is a pointer in the range [i.first, i.last).  NOTE:
 734:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *      the implication of this is that i.cur is always a dereferenceable
 735:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *      pointer, even if i is a past-the-end iterator.
 736:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * - Start and Finish are always nonsingular iterators.  NOTE: this
 737:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * means that an empty deque must have one node, a deque with <N
 738:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * elements (where N is the node buffer size) must have one node, a
 739:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * deque with N through (2N-1) elements must have two nodes, etc.
 740:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * - For every node other than start.node and finish.node, every
 741:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * element in the node is an initialized object.  If start.node ==
 742:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * finish.node, then [start.cur, finish.cur) are initialized
 743:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * objects, and the elements outside that range are uninitialized
 744:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * storage.  Otherwise, [start.cur, start.last) and [finish.first,
 745:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * finish.cur) are initialized objects, and [start.first, start.cur)
 746:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * and [finish.cur, finish.last) are uninitialized storage.
 747:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * - [%map, %map + map_size) is a valid, non-empty range.
 748:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    * - [start.node, finish.node] is a valid range contained within
 749:/Library/DaisyToolchain/0.2.0/arm/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/10.3.1/bits/stl_deque.h ****    *   [%map, %map + map_size).
